  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "'चाहिए' is a unique verb form in Hindi that is not related to 'चाहना'. Its subject, if expressed, is marked by the postposition 'को'. With a noun, 'चाहिए' means 'need', as in 'आपको क्या चाहिए?' meaning 'What do you need?' or 'मुझे काम चाहिए' meaning 'I need a job'.\nWhen used with an infinitive, 'चाहिए' expresses 'should' or 'ought to'. For example, 'हमें जाना चाहिए' means 'We should go'.\nIf the direct object of the verb is mentioned in the direct case, the infinitive agrees with it: 'हमको हिन्दी सीखनी चाहिए' means 'We ought to learn Hindi', and 'आपको नये जूते खरीदने चाहिए' means 'You should buy new shoes'. However, many speakers do not make this agreement and might say 'हिन्दी सीखना चाहिए' or 'जूते खरीदना चाहिए'.\nSome speakers use a plural form 'चाहियेँ' when talking about plural objects, as in 'उन्हें किताबें खरीदनी चाहिएँ' (They ought to buy books).\nIn all cases, the concept of need or obligation still refers back to the subject, which is marked by 'को'.\nFor example, 'हमें अपने काम के बारे में बोलना चाहिए' means 'We should speak about our work'."
    }
